  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 17 Chapter 487\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4049-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the executive law, in relation to the performance\n        of a study regarding homeless persons who are  veterans  in  the\n        state of New York\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  require  the Division of Veterans' Services (\"Divi-\nsion\") to conduct a study to determine the number of homeless persons in\nNew York state that are veterans, as well  as  the  number  of  homeless\nchildren  of veterans. The U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs currently\nconducts a point-in-time count to statistically determine the number  of\nsheltered and unsheltered homeless veterans in each state. Additionally,\nthe  U.S.  Department  of Housing and Urban Development issues an Annual\nHomeless Assessment Report (AHAR) that addresses this issue.\n \n  Therefore I have reached an agreement with the  Legislature  to  amend\nthis  legislation  in  the  upcoming  session to address this concern by\nallowing the Division to prepare a report for  the  Legislature  consol-\nidating the information that has been gathered by other entities includ-\ning local veterans services agencies, which will increase efficiency and\nstill  provide an avenue to report on this information. On that basis, I\nam signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2019
 },
